B.a_T=new A.R("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Somebody drenched her, Detective \u2014 gallons of scalding espresso, poured until she went soggy and simply fell apart. We outlined what was left in powdered sugar.",B.f,B.f)
B.a0b=new A.R("weapon","What was the weapon?","That brass espresso urn lying on its side. Take a good look at it.",B.f,B.f)
B.KN=s(["urn"],t.s)
B.a0A=new A.R("weight","How heavy is that urn?","Full? Glaze and I tried to right it between us and nearly lost our icing. I had a go on my own first. Couldn't get one side off the floor.",B.KN,B.f)
B.HZ=s([B.a_T,B.a0b,B.a0A,B.ky],t.q)
B.a_G=new A.R("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She'd been upset lately \u2014 her pearls went missing last month, and she'd been shut up with her solicitor ever since.",B.f,B.f)
B.a_l=new A.R("suspect","Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but the Colonel owes Madam a fortune, and Barry was in her bad books over the strawberries.",B.f,B.f)
B.j6=s(["graham/where"],t.s)
B.a_o=new A.R("dark","Graham says he and Tira were counting silver next door.","Last night? The dining room is right through that wall, Detective. From half ten on it was dark and silent as a fridge. No light under the door, not a clink. And you can't count a hundred and forty-four pieces of silver without a clink.",B.f,B.j6)
B.nC=s(["graham/dark"],t.s)
B.a_L=new A.R("lamp","Graham says they worked by a shaded lamp.","A lamp? The only lamp on this floor is the one on my kitchen table, and it never left my sight. I was reading my basting times by it.",B.f,B.nC)
B.nK=s(["silver"],t.s)
B.a0q=new A.R("silver","Your tag says you counted the silver at 3 PM.","Every piece, and polished it too. It's counted on the first of the month, and that was yesterday afternoon. Nobody had any call to count it again that night.",B.nK,B.f)
B.nx=s(["candles"],t.s)
B.a0_=new A.R("candles",u.b,"I should think not, I only put them in yesterday afternoon. Still white, are they? Then nobody has had a light on in that room since.",B.nx,B.f)
B.a_R=new A.R("cocoa","Did Tira fetch port from the cellar at nine?","She did, that much is true. Whether nine was the only time she went down, I couldn't tell you. I had my head in an oven.",B.j2,B.f)
B.a_u=new A.R("boom","Could you hear the Colonel on the telephone?","Hear him? The whole county could. He was bellowing about the Battle of Blancmange for the best part of an hour. It came down the stairwell like a brass band.",B.f,B.ns)
B.KU=s([B.ko,B.a_G,B.a_l,B.a_o,B.a_L,B.a0q,B.a0_,B.a_R,B.a_u,B.km,B.zg,B.kt,B.kw,B.kq],t.q)
B.a0c=new A.R("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the dining room, sir, conducting the silver inventory with Miss Tira's kind assistance. Half past ten until half past eleven. One hundred and forty-four pieces, all present.",B.f,B.f)
B.a08=new A.R("suspect","Who do you suspect?","It is not a butler's place to speculate, sir. I will observe only that the Colonel is deeply in debt to Madam.",B.f,B.f)
B.nq=s(["penny/dark"],t.s)
B.a_B=new A.R("dark",u.p,"We worked by a single shaded lamp, sir, so as not to disturb the house. And one lays silver down on baize. It makes no sound.",B.f,B.nq)
B.a_Q=new A.R("silver","Penny had already counted the silver at 3 PM.","Mrs. Cotta counts, sir. I verify. It is the difference between a housekeeper and a butler.",B.nK,B.f)
B.a_F=new A.R("candles",u.b,"As I say, sir, we did not use the chandelier. One does not burn Madam's good candles to count spoons.",B.nx,B.f)
B.Kc=s(["notepad"],t.s)
B.a_m=new A.R("notepad","What did you write on the missing sheet?","A reminder to wind the hall clock, sir. Tonight, at eleven. It keeps poor time if one is late.",B.Kc,B.f)
B.nF=s(["note"],t.s)
B.a_v=new A.R("note","This burnt note is on your monogrammed paper.","Madam's paper, sir, not mine. There is a pad of it in every room of this house. Anyone might have used it.",B.nF,B.f)
B.nE=s(["newwill","solicitor"],t.s)
B.a0a=new A.R("will","She was dismissing you without a pension.","Madam said nothing of the kind to me, sir. One would naturally be distressed, after thirty years.",B.nE,B.f)
B.nM=s(["tickets"],t.s)
B.a0n=new A.R("tickets","Two tickets to Biscotti Bay, Graham?","A holiday, sir, long planned. Miss Tira dislikes queues and asked me to purchase her ticket along with my own. That is all.",B.nM,B.f)
B.nH=s(["pearls"],t.s)
B.a0w=new A.R("pearls","What happened to the Senclair pearls?","Mislaid, sir. Madam was forever mislaying things. I could not say how a pawn ticket came to be in the case.",B.nH,B.f)
B.Iz=s([B.a0c,B.kk,B.a08,B.a_B,B.a_Q,B.a_F,B.a_m,B.a_v,B.a0a,B.a0n,B.a0w,B.kl,B.kv,B.kx],t.q)
B.a_D=new A.R("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Helping Graham count the silver in the dining room, darling. Half ten to half eleven. Frightfully dull \u2014 spoons, spoons, spoons.",B.f,B.f)
B.a_Z=new A.R("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Aunt \xc9claire was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. We adored each other. Everyone knows I am her sole heir.",B.f,B.f)
B.a_t=new A.R("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The Colonel, darling. He owes her mountains of sugar. Or that muddy little gardener she was about to sack.",B.f,B.f)
B.a0h=new A.R("dark",u.p,"Penny had her head in an oven, darling. She wouldn't have noticed a brass band marching through the hall.",B.f,B.nq)
B.a0f=new A.R("lamp","Where did the lamp you worked by come from?","Lamp? We had the chandelier blazing, darling, one can't count spoons in the gloom. ...Why, what did Graham say?",B.f,B.nC)
B.JO=s(["gloves"],t.s)
B.a0j=new A.R("gloves","Your gloves are soaked in espresso.","I spilled my after-dinner coffee, darling. All of it. I'm a tiramisu; we're practically made of coffee. I hid them because Auntie paid for them and would have shrieked.",B.JO,B.f)
B.a01=new A.R("will","Your aunt was cutting you out of her will.","Auntie rewrote her will every time her bunions ached, darling, and tore it up again by Friday. Nobody took it seriously. Least of all me.",B.nE,B.f)
B.a_w=new A.R("tickets","You have a train ticket to Biscotti Bay for tonight.","A little seaside air, darling, for my nerves. Graham queued for me. Is a girl not allowed a holiday?",B.nM,B.f)
B.a05=new A.R("pearls","What happened to the Senclair pearls?","Auntie lost them, found them, lost them again. I never touched the ugly things.",B.nH,B.f)
B.JM=s([B.a_D,B.a_Z,B.a_t,B.a0h,B.a0f,B.a0j,B.a01,B.a_w,B.a05,B.kz],t.q)
B.a_y=new A.R("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the attic landing, sir! Ten to eleven until half past, swapping war stories with old Major Meringue at the Fort Fondant Officers' Club.",B.f,B.f)
B.z0=new A.R("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? Splendid woman. Very patient with a chap's temporary financial embarrassments.",B.f,B.f)
B.a0k=new A.R("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The housekeeper found the body, sir. In my experience the chap who finds the body wants watching. Or the gardener. Never trust a tart.",B.f,B.f)
B.a0l=new A.R("dining","Did you pass the dining room last night?","Came down the stairs at half past eleven when I rang off, sir, straight past it. Door shut, no light under it, quiet as a churchyard. Why, was somebody meant to be in there?",B.f,B.j6)
B.j7=s(["ricottadrip"],t.s)
B.a0d=new A.R("drip","There is ricotta on the floor by the telephone.","I stood on that spot for forty minutes, sir. A chap drips. Old war wound. I'd be more worried if there were none.",B.j7,B.f)
B.K_=s(["iou"],t.s)
B.zb=new A.R("iou","You owed her 50,000 sugar cubes.","I did, and I do, and I'm not proud of it. But she had given me until Christmas, and a dead creditor's heirs are far less patient. Her death is the worst thing that could happen to my finances, what!",B.K_,B.f)
B.KC=s(["sabre"],t.s)
B.z3=new A.R("sabre","Your sabre is in the attic, and it is sticky.","Toffee apples, sir! Fearsome things to slice. I was carving one for myself on Sunday, the blade stuck fast in that dummy, and I haven't had the puff to pull it out since.",B.KC,B.f)
B.KV=s([B.a_y,B.z0,B.a0k,B.a0l,B.a0d,B.zb,B.z3],t.q)
B.a0t=new A.R("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Couldn't say, guv. But whoever it was had a strong back. I haul coal all day and I can't shift that coffee urn on me own.",B.f,B.f)
B.a_i=new A.R("furnace","I pulled a burnt note out of your furnace.","Ain't my writin', guv \u2014 I can barely spell \u201cfertiliser\u201d. But when I came in at midnight the furnace door was open and the fire fresh-poked. I banked it meself at six. Somebody had been at it.",B.nF,B.f)
